			"holiday_rest_precedence": "REST_DAY",
			"authority": "Peraturan Pemerintah No. 35 Tahun 2021 Pasal 27(1) — an employer who employs a worker beyond the Pasal 21(2) working hours must pay overtime wages; the regulation sets no wage threshold, and its only exception (Pasal 27(2)) is by job group, which this workspace cannot yet express. Pasal 26(1) caps overtime at 4 hours in a day and 18 hours in a week, and Pasal 26(2) puts overtime worked on a weekly rest day or an official public holiday outside that cap. Undang-Undang No. 13 Tahun 2003 Pasal 79(2)(a) as amended by Undang-Undang No. 6 Tahun 2023 gives a break of at least 30 minutes after 4 continuous hours, not counted as working time, and Pasal 79(2)(b) one rest day for every 6 working days in a week."
